#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Replace a legacy sandbox bootstrap after a proved whole-sandbox stop
(--stop-legacy), or take a new release into a sandbox the containerised
supervisor already looks after (--upgrade, and --upgrade --back to put the
saved previous installation back). An upgrade runs with the Compose
sandbox-runner stopped (exit 0) and never stops the sandbox, moves a port or
policy rule, or unmasks a unit; it saves the previous template, profile,
settings file and clone-local git identity to
<evidence_dir>/previous-installation/ (0600, with hashes; the previous
bootstrap env, which carries secrets, by its hash only) before changing
anything, and writes sandbox-installed.json format 2 with a previous block.
--upgrade and --upgrade --back each have one overall time limit
(UPGRADE_LIMIT_SECONDS, 1500): every command they run is bounded by what is
left of it, and none is started after it.

Private inventory: common project/env_file/runtime_image/docker_context and units
runner/keeper, plus sandbox:{name, clone_path, known_files, receipts_path,
script_path, profile_path, profile_source, systemd_user_dir, evidence_dir,
remote_ref, remote_name, declared_remote, declaration_files, release_image,
expected_sbx_version, legacy_dropins, legacy_command_markers, forbidden_values,
settings_path, repo_keys, worktree_disk_floor_gb} and volumes.settings (the
coordinator's settings volume, read only through a read-only helper container).
The sandbox's own settings file (release -3 TC5) is generated from the
coordinator's settings and holds only what the in-sandbox helper and runner
read; FORGE_CONFIG_PATH in the bootstrap env names it.
Routes come ONLY from the explicit env file: FACTORY_GATEWAY_ADDRESS,
FORGE_TARGET_OWNER_URL, FORGE_SANDBOX_SIDECAR_URL, FORGE_SANDBOX_RUNNER_URL,
FLEET_MEMORY_PORT (the memory MCP's gateway publish port, as compose.yaml uses it).
The producer profile retains all choices except gateway publish addresses,
explicit allow-rule replacements, receipts_path and cwd. sandbox.allow_replacements
maps old host:port entries to env variable NAMES holding replacement host:port.
No shell sourcing, ambient route overrides or broker clients.
"""
